{"id": "EUVD-2026-76511", "enisaUuid": "b0af733b-022c-3abb-96fc-059fd36b5924", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfbdev: omapfb: panel-dsi-cm: initialize lock before registering display\n\ndsicm_probe() registers the display before initializing ddata->lock.\nOnce omapdss_register_display() publishes the display, another consumer\ncan reach a dsicm callback that takes this mutex while it is still\nuninitialized.\n\nInitialize the mutex before registering the display so the published\ncallbacks always see a valid lock.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:49:31", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef20d4e17d7fb0d83144caa9667e6f3198288993", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7023d18c4eb292f886b31a3576402cb0e357df7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f33a96e49284589257e90ddc4394ec0c6bf11ec4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/302d19fbc7dc7e9f498930c66d65ff711ba5ba9f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c3f8c9c995db185284b079f39177e85b2258176", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/76818e81cfcae33b09b739de09162c7d8d89bf0b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/09db79078f25c048cfb5d7849795c70415ab8574", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f8e43fe0f22b7137ce456e6fe3581d3098174f74"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vq32-rv69-wv5x", "CVE-2026-89599"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cf47219-456a-327b-b7d3-4ad5627c59bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f76ee892a99e68b55402b8d4b8aeffcae2aff34d <f33a96e49284589257e90ddc4394ec0c6bf11ec4"}, {"id": "0d795e49-60e8-3181-ad82-de030e70a58f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f76ee892a99e68b55402b8d4b8aeffcae2aff34d <2c3f8c9c995db185284b079f39177e85b2258176"}, {"id": "0e6d6ffe-587e-317d-9af4-78b442d1be3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "